# Line endings, settled once.
#
# This repo drifted into mixed endings: twelve tracked text files were CRLF and
# the rest LF, with no rule saying which was right. That turned any tool doing a
# read-modify-write into a hazard — a four-line edit to mcp/AGENTS.md landed as a
# 474-line diff purely because the write normalised its endings, which buries the
# real change in review and in `git log -p` permanently. It happened four times.
#
# LF everywhere in the repository. This is a Linux-hosted Node/Astro project built
# on a Pi and deployed by Vercel; nothing here needs CRLF, and the CRLF files were
# an accident of which editor touched them, not a decision.
#
# Applied to the existing history with:  git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Diffing it is noise, and it is rebuilt by `pnpm --filter mcp-gui build:css`.
mcp/gui/public/app.css linguist-generated=true
mcp/gui/styles/icons.css linguist-generated=true

# Lockfile: keep it out of diffs and merge conflicts you would hand-resolve.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true
